      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PETES BIG JIM (7) settled handy then took over in front and fought hard all the way to the line to finish second last start over 1710m at Goulburn, the second podium finish in succession. Drawn to enjoy a cosy run but might need things to go his way at some stage. Meets a comparable field and he is a strong winning hope. FREASON (10) produced a good effort at his latest appearance to get home by a narrow margin over 1710m at Goulburn on September 7. Not drawn to best so may need a 10/10 drive. Won't find this any harder and he can go right on with the job. JEKAMIAS NZ (2) didn't do a bad job when fifth over 1740m at Riverina Paceway last time out. THE TALK (1) should not have any excuses from the favourable draw.",
